Dana, our formal position on SR-014 is attached on letterhead. The short ve=
rsion is below so there is no ambiguity in the email record either.<br />
<br />
VAA recommends against deleting Section 09 05 61. The in-situ relative humi=
dity measured at depth is 92 to 96% against a specification threshold of 85=
%. Installing resilient flooring and adhesive over a slab in that condition=
, with no vapor barrier, will in our professional judgment lead to adhesive=
 breakdown, bond failure and lifting of the flooring, and creates a risk of=
 microbial growth beneath the assembly. The failure is not immediate. Acros=
s the general office areas it typically appears somewhere between eight and=
 fifteen years into the installation, which is well past any warranty eithe=
r of us will be holding. The wet-use rooms are the exception and will go so=
oner, inside the first two to four years, because heat welded sheet is effe=
ctively impermeable and the room adds its own water at the surface. On this=
 job that means the pantries and the Level 19 wellness room.<br />
<br />
We understand the budget and the schedule pressure and we are not disputing=
 that the credit is real. What we are saying is that the credit is $347,900=
 today against a repair that will cost multiples of that later, and that th=
e decision is the Owner's to make and not ours.<br />
<br />
If Ardsley elects to proceed with the deletion, VAA will issue the ASI, but=
 we will issue it only on written direction from Ardsley that records the d=
eletion as owner-directed and made over our written recommendation. Please =
confirm in writing if that is the direction you want.
--00450cb5821ae1686bed2432393d3c9a1e59c31cb18c65999f7befba3932
